      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. I like the contrast. \n\nBut for the second monologue—the local resident—it feels a little too abstract/weird with the \"locusts\" and \"water jug\" thing. I want it to feel more grounded and \"real.\" Usually, when people talk about these older, established neighborhoods, there's a certain way the people speak that's a bit more gritty or unpolished, especially if they're struggling with the changes.\n\nCan you rewrite the second one? Try to make their speech pattern sound a bit more \"street\" or less academic, maybe use some more common slang or a more aggressive, defensive tone to show how they feel about the newcomers taking over. Make it feel like someone who's seen it all and isn't impressed by the new crowd.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
